  "body": "Reported via Discord on 2026-11-17 (relayed by Mike): CamCraft v0.23.0 on Windows 11 \"kept crashing\"; the user uninstalled it. Details since:\n- Desktop PC, AMD Ryzen 5, onboard (integrated) Radeon graphics; the board has no dedicated video memory.\n- \"Crash\" means the whole computer: the picture turns to \"snow\", then the PC locks up and needs a hard reset. The user also has trouble with local AI applications on the same PC.\n\nReading: a graphics driver or hardware hang under GPU load (integrated graphics use main RAM, so RAM instability shows as snow then a lock-up), not an app crash. CamCraft ran fine on three other Windows 11 machines (NVIDIA, Intel, Parallels ARM VM).\n\nAsked the user for: `dxdiag` \"Save All Information\" (driver version and date, exact CPU model); a test with XMP/EXPO off and \"UMA Frame Buffer Size\" 2-4 GB; the latest AMD Adrenalin driver; optionally OCCT 3D / MemTest86.\n\n**Waiting for the user.** Closed on or after 2026-11-25 if there is no answer. Related: #2421 (log + safe graphics mode), #2423 (Windows troubleshooting page).\n",
